From 8ecc9784460a1920d8220a9e9df3617d934bb242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein-work <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:50:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Restructure into the pluggable-backend package shape
 (keras_tinygrad.src)

The backend sources move from `_backend/` (flat, served under a
`keras.src.backend.tinygrad` alias by the import hook, re-exported for
keras' pluggable_backend branch by an aliasing shim) to
`keras_tinygrad/src/` in the layout keras' in-tree backends and the
split-out keras-team/keras-openvino / keras-mlx packages use:
`ops/{core,image,linalg,math,nn,numpy}.py`, `random.py`, `rnn.py`,
`trainer.py`, `layer.py`, `export.py`. Internal imports are
`keras_tinygrad.src.*`. `Variable` stays in `ops/core.py`, where keras'
in-tree backends keep it (keras-openvino's separate `variable.py` is that
package's choice, not protocol).

The package `__init__` exports both spellings, the `ops` subpackage that
keras >= 3.16 reads (`backend.ops.numpy.x`) and the flat module names
that 3.15.x reads (`backend.numpy.x`), so one package serves both.

The alias is gone. The loader's six patches import `keras_tinygrad.src`
directly, exactly what the branch resolves for `keras_<name>.src`; stock
keras 3.15.1 never builds a backend module name dynamically, so those six
import sites are the only places the backend is named, and
`keras.src.backend.tinygrad` no longer exists (asserted by the loader
test, together with module identity for all six ops modules under both
spellings). The loader keeps one job: the exact-once anchor patches.

`ops/__init__.py` star-imports `core` FIRST and binds the submodules with
plain `import keras_tinygrad.src.ops.x` statements: `core` has a bare
`import math` that the star import re-exports as `ops.math`, and a later
`from keras_tinygrad.src.ops import math` would return that stdlib
attribute without loading the submodule.

`export.py` (the real module now) carries a guarded
`SavedModelExportArchive` for the branch protocol, a subclass of
`BaseSavedModelExportArchive` when that base is importable, absent on
3.15.x where keras subclasses `TinygradExportArchive` itself; `layer.py`
carries `BackendLayer`, `trainer.py` `Trainer`.

Packaging: entry point `keras_tinygrad.src`, no more `_backend`
package-data (the wheel ships 18 modules), ruff exclusion moved to the
new directory (the backend sources stay in keras' in-tree style, never
reformatted). CI byte-compiles the new paths. Docs updated in the same
diff (README, CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING, HANDOFF, how-it-works,
architecture, the 2026-09-21 status note, path mentions).

Verified: make verify (48 passed), make smoke, make vendor-check, make
readme-check, make tutorial, the CI byte-compile step, a wheel build, and
a branch-style `import keras_tinygrad.src` without the hook under the
numpy backend.

